  "decisions": [
    "Accept all28 fixed raw in-zone visual reference boxes:27 PRQ and one PBR. They surround distinct elongated vessel responses at native resolution; do not enlarge boxes toward detector geometry. All physical attributes remain null.",
    "Keep every clearly resolved context vessel whose centroid is outside the active AOIs outside the local reference count, including the Apr3 white inner-basin hull. No AOI adjustment to capture extra positives.",
    "Keep STC Apr3 double-lobe quay response unknown: the raw image does not reliably distinguish one hull, two hulls or infrastructure. Apr13 cloudy waterfront remains unreviewable; three observations abstain completely.",
    "Keep both small native PRQ water signatures unknown rather than declaring false positives or inventing positive hull boxes. Root independently noticed the Apr13 signature in the harbor raw before its correspondence was disclosed. The Apr13 faint offshore trace around(285,198) is outside all active zones, as checked separately.",
    "Accept the separately documented scope guard addendum to remove footprints of unresolved proposals. This exclusion is explicitly conditioned on detector geometry; it removes12.47%,8.56%,12.05% from the three respective raw scopes and limits generalization. Raw scope artifacts are retained; no removed area is counted as a negative. This guarded test does not support an unconditional full-port performance claim.",
    "Keep automatic masks and numerical rasters unchanged. Restrict cloud-day negatives to inspected clear subareas. Calibration/test hypotheses remain fixed, and this small test cohort cannot satisfy the fixed support gate."
  ]
